From eb0c4403f113abefdd8d5aca0267a961ed3cda9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:02:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: ps_guest_pixel_center_shaders, passes drawn as the
 console draws them

The Vulkan side of f1790e0. Pixel shaders listed in
ps_guest_pixel_center_shaders are moved up and left by (scale minus 1) / 2
host pixels through the NDC offset, and every other host pixel of a guest
pixel takes the first one's interpolants along the fine derivatives.

Three things differ from Direct3D 12. NDC Y points down here, along render
target Y, so both axes subtract. The cvar and its hash check lived in
dxbc_translator.cpp, which only Direct3D 12 builds compile, so on Linux the
setting the games make was dropped without a word: both move to
translator.cpp. And the fragment shader now asks for gl_FragCoord itself,
since these passes run with early fragment tests and nothing else did.

Checked on lavapipe at 2x in Trials Evolution's own page table pass, with
its fetch result replaced by a hash of the coordinates it computed (the
Vulkan page table holds no real data yet: integer number format fetches
and resolves exist only on Direct3D 12). All three dumps match 1x in every
guest texel of levels 3 to 7, and no guest texel has host pixels that
differ. With the cvar off 5516 texels differ, and with the Direct3D 12 sign
on Y all 5516 come out wrong.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
